---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const updated = '3 August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Wander"
  description="Privacy Policy for the Wander app and website."
>
  <article class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container-site max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">1. Overview</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            This Privacy Policy explains how Wander (“we”, “us”) collects, uses, and shares information
            when you use the Wander app and {site.url}.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">2. Information we collect</h2>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-ink">Account data</strong> — such as email address, when you create an account.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-ink">Project data</strong> — routes, styles, and settings you create in the app,
              stored so you can reopen and export projects.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-ink">Purchase data</strong> — subscription status via Apple, Google, and our
              payments provider (e.g. RevenueCat). We do not receive your full payment card details.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-ink">Device and usage data</strong> — approximate diagnostics needed to run and
              improve the Service (for example crash reports, if enabled).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-ink">Support messages</strong> — content you send to {site.supportEmail}.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">3. How we use information</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We use information to provide and improve Wander, process subscriptions, authenticate accounts,
            respond to support requests, and meet legal obligations. We do not sell your personal information.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">4. Sharing</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We share data with service providers who help us operate the Service (for example hosting,
            authentication, analytics, and subscription management), only as needed for those purposes.
            We may disclose information if required by law or to protect rights and safety.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">5. Retention</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We retain account and project data while your account is active and as needed to provide the
            Service. You may request deletion by contacting us; some records may be kept where legally required.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">6. Security</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your information. No method
            of transmission or storage is completely secure.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">7. Children</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Wander is not directed at children under 13 (or the minimum age in your jurisdiction). We do not
            knowingly collect personal information from children.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">8. Your rights</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or export your
            personal data, or to object to certain processing. Contact us to make a request.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">9. Changes</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We may update this policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top will change when
            we do. Continued use of the Service after updates constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">10. Contact</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Privacy questions: <a class="text-primary font-medium" href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
